    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1405" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŭla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŏl-</span></b> ), ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town in the neighborhood of Tibur</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				29, 6</span></i> (Aefula, Müll.); cf. Müll. Roms
			Campagn. 1, 272.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŭlānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>pertaining to
			Æsula</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arx,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 9</span></i>
			 Madv.; and <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŏlāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Æsula</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 69</span></i> Jan.</div>
